course: dictionary
lesson: 540
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Good readers use context, the words around the word, to find the right meaning. «Picture a class atlas open at Asia» tells you that an atlas is something you open and look at. You open a book of maps, so atlas means a book of maps here.
explain: Atlas can also be a name with a capital letter. In Greek myths, Atlas is a giant who holds up the sky on his shoulders. A book cannot hold up the sky, so the sentence «Atlas holds up the sky» is talking about a person, not a book.
explain: Atlas can also be a science word. The atlas is the top bone of the spine, and it holds up your head. Here «the atlas» is a part of the body, so you know it is not a book or a giant.
fact: An atlas is a book of maps. The plural is atlases.
fact: Atlas is a giant in Greek myths who holds up the sky on his shoulders.
fact: The atlas is the top bone of your spine, which holds up your head.
fact: «The atlas moth» is one of the biggest moths, as big as a plate.
fact: Check the clues first: a capital letter, a body part, or a sentence about maps can all tell you which meaning is right.
exercise: «Picture a class atlas open at Asia.» In this sentence, what is an atlas? | A giant holding up the sky | A bone in the neck | A type of plant | *A book of maps
exercise: In Greek myths, what does Atlas do? | Eats giant moths | Draws maps for sailors | Swims across the sea | *Holds up the sky on his shoulders
exercise: «The atlas moth is one of the biggest moths.» What kind of word is atlas in this sentence? | A giant in myths | *The name of a type of moth | A book of maps | The top bone of the spine
test: Maya checked the atlas to find the capital city of France. What is an atlas here? | A giant who holds up the sky | A kind of moth | *A book of maps | The top bone of the spine
test: Ben says the atlas holds up his head. Which meaning of atlas is Ben using? | A giant in Greek myths | A type of moth | *The top bone of the spine | A book of maps
exam: Why is Atlas in «Atlas holds up the sky on his shoulders» a name and not a book of maps? | Because all atlases are heavy | *Because it has a capital letter and holds up the sky, which a book cannot do | Because it is spelled wrongly
